## What it does

`apps/mischief` hosts the public documentation and agent interfaces.

- Discovery cards describe MCP and A2A.
- [OpenAPI](/openapi.json) describes the HTTP capability surface.
- The [agent guide](/llms.txt) explains connection, search, read, and graph traversal.
- The hosted registry exposes `search`, `read`, `backlinks`, `neighbors`, `mentions`, `path`, and `execute`.

### Run a program instead of several calls

Use `POST /api/execute` with a JSON `code` string. The MCP `execute` tool runs the same job.

[Code mode](/lore/one-program-can-replace-several-tool-calls) runs content capabilities in one program. `joinInterest` stays outside the sandbox.

Source: callable definitions in [`apps/mischief/src/capabilities/index.ts` at `445b1a20b51a5492f8e586daeb9306e8011b7673`, lines 34–45](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-stack/blob/445b1a20b51a5492f8e586daeb9306e8011b7673/apps/mischief/src/capabilities/index.ts#L34-L45).

```js
const found = await tools.search({ query: "cartridges", limit: 1 });
const page = await tools.read({ id: found.matches[0].id });
return { title: page.title, id: page.id };
```

**What to notice:** The program passes the search result directly to read.

MCP supports protocol versions 2026-07-28, 2025-11-25, 2025-06-18, 2025-03-26, and 2024-11-05. The newest is stateless. Older clients initialize sessions backed by a Durable Object.

A2A answers documentation questions through search and read. Browser RPC is a separate projection, not another agent interface.

## The standard

- Domain calls use shared capability schemas and handlers.
- Discovery and static pages are routing, not extra domain handlers.
- Public API access needs no account or access token.
- [Interest signup](/systems/interest) has its own consent and confirmation boundary.
- `execute` runs an async function body in a fresh Dynamic Worker with `globalOutbound: null`.
- Imports, exports, and `fetch` are unavailable.
- The program calls declared capabilities, not arbitrary network services.
- API and MCP allow 120 requests per IP per 60 seconds.
- Execute also allows 6 per IP and 300 total per 60 seconds.
- Native Cloudflare counters apply separately per location.

These routes exist today. A generic front-door cartridge remains planned.

## How to check

1. Read the [MCP connection card](/.well-known/mcp.json).
2. Read the [A2A card](/.well-known/agent-card.json).
3. Read [OpenAPI](/openapi.json).
4. Compare the descriptions with `apps/mischief/src/capabilities/index.ts`.
5. Use the `tools/list` request in [llms.txt](/llms.txt).
6. Search for a public document.
7. Read the document.
8. Run `pnpm --filter @rat-stack/mischief test` for protocol routing, rate limiting, and sandbox behavior.
9. Confirm the live cards and capability list before advertising a new agent path.

Local tests do not prove a new deploy.
